{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "id": "onprem-physical-logical",
    "title": "On-premises physical and logical reference",
    "environment": "reference",
    "assumptions": [
      "Synthetic reference model: nothing here describes deployed infrastructure. Every name, ID, VLAN number and address range is invented for illustration.",
      "The brief supplied no cabling, routing, storage-path or traffic flows, so the infrastructure part declares no relationships. Only the Kubernetes links the brief names are drawn.",
      "The site, data center, room, three racks and each device's rack are chosen here; the brief asked only for a data center with at least two racks.",
      "Network, VRF, VLAN, subnet and security-zone names, numbers and CIDR ranges, and each device's membership in them, are authored for this reference.",
      "Two networks (production and management) are modeled so that the router, L3 switch, firewall, hypervisor and VM 1 each belong to more than one network.",
      "Both VMs declare the single hypervisor as their host. No compute-cluster boundary is modeled because the brief names one hypervisor only.",
      "The physical server is a separate bare-metal host. It is not declared to run the hypervisor or any VM, and the brief states no workload for it.",
      "Database, NAS, SAN, identity, backup and monitoring are placed as rack-mounted devices on IP subnets. A storage fabric such as Fibre Channel is not modeled.",
      "The Kubernetes cluster is user-managed, one entity in every view, attached to the application subnet and zone. No node pool or control plane is modeled, and Nodes declare no pool.",
      "The Nodes' host VM or server and their subnets are not supplied, so the Nodes carry no placement outside the cluster.",
      "The Deployment has two replicas matching two Pods, one on each Node. Names such as worker-1, web and app are invented for this reference.",
      "The Ingress controller is cluster-level with no declared namespace. The NetworkPolicy is declared to apply to the Deployment's Pods and defines no rules.",
      "The Deployment claims the PVC, which is bound to a PV with a StorageClass. The PV backing store is not supplied and is not linked to the NAS or SAN.",
      "The Secret is a reference only. No value, key or data is stored in the model.",
      "The physical view also selects the networks, subnets and security zones, only so that devices show their logical memberships as notes.",
      "The logical view also selects the racks, only so that devices show their rack placement as notes. VMs and the cluster declare the site, not a rack, so the physical view draws them in the site outside any rack."
    ],
    "description": "Synthetic T-005 reference: one data center modeled once, drawn as separate physical, logical and Kubernetes views that share resource IDs."
  },
